hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15529","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, he said: Isa ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydillah informed me, from Umayr ibn Salamah al-Damri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Arj, and there was a hamstrung donkey, and it was not long before a man of Bahz came and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my shot, so dispose of it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and he divided it among the companies. Then he marched until he came to Aqabat Uthayah, and there was a gazelle with an arrow in it, crouching in the shade of a rock. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man of his Companions and said: Stand here until the companies pass, let none shoot it with anything."
